# Turbo
.turbo/

# Environment
#
# `.env.*` rather than an enumerated list: the previous three rules covered `.env`,
# `.env.local` and `.env.*.local`, which left every other suffix committable. A real
# `.env.ec3` holding `JWT_SECRET`, `COOKIE_SECRET`, `KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET`,
# `S3_SECRET_KEY` and `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN` was sitting untracked-but-not-ignored in a
# working tree, one `git add .` away from being committed. `.env.production`,
# `.env.staging` and `.env.test` had the same gap.
#
# `.env.example` is negated because it is the tracked template and contains only
# placeholder values. Keep it that way: anything added to it must not be a real secret.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

